10
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
City Slickers is a 1991 American Western comedy film directed by Ron Underwood and starring Billy Crystal, Daniel Stern, Bruno Kirby and Jack
Palance, with supporting roles by Patricia Wettig, Helen Slater, Noble Willingham and Jake Gyllenhaal making his acting debut.

11
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:46,000
The film's screenplay was written by Lowell Ganz and Babaloo Mandel, and it was
shot in New York City, New Mexico, Durango, Colorado, and Spain.

12
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
City Slickers was released by Columbia Pictures on June 7, 1991.

13
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
The film received positive reviews from critics and grossed
$179 million against a $26 million budget.

14
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
For his performance, Palance won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor.

15
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
A sequel titled The Legend of Curly's Gold was released in 1994 with the same cast, with
the exception of Kirby, who was replaced by Jon Lovitz in a different role.

16
01:41:20,000 --> 01:41:26,000
The film explores themes of stetson, vacation, cattle
drive, prairie, fish out of water.

17
01:47:40,000 --> 01:47:46,000
The tone is lighthearted.
